# Design Planner credentials — the LLM that plans an empty room's furniture.
#
# Copy this file to .dardesign-llm (gitignored) and fill it in, then restart
# scripts\run-local-backend.ps1.
#
# UNCONFIGURED IS A WORKING MODE. With no key the planner returns a layout
# computed from DAR's own placement rules and labels it "Planned by DAR's
# rules" in the UI. The demo, the tests and CI all run that path, so nothing
# is dark without a key.
#
# A Pro/Plus web subscription is NOT API access. This key comes from
# console.anthropic.com (pay-as-you-go).
#
# Cost: the catalogue is 9 items per culture, so a plan is roughly 1k tokens in
# and 1.5k out — about $0.02 on Sonnet 5, less on Haiku. Repeated briefs are
# served from an in-process cache and cost nothing. The backend also refuses to
# make more than 200 calls per process, and logs the estimated cost of each.

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Optional. Defaults to claude-sonnet-5.
#   claude-haiku-4-5  — cheapest, ~$0.004 a plan
#   claude-sonnet-5   — the default; best value for structured planning
#   claude-opus-5     — strongest spatial reasoning, ~$0.02-0.05 a plan
# DARDESIGN_LLM_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
